  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "Alex J. Adams said predictive analytics in child welfare should focus on decision support rather than decision making and should not replace decisions by skilled human staff. He also said agencies should aim to minimize the risk of bias in all their decisions. Adams said he liked that a presidential executive order discussed the use of AI or predictive analytics. In an ACF press release, Adams described child welfare caseworkers as making high-stakes decisions under pressure and said promising county-level use cases could be scaled at the state level to improve outcomes.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s2",
    "s3",
    "s4",
    "s5"
   ],
